<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄτοβ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any loud noise</i>, as <i>the
				din</i> of battle, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. ἄπλητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Th.</u>
					709
				</span></i>
			; <i>rattling</i> of chariots, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				151
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				204
			</span></i> (both lyr.); <i>crash</i> of thunder, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1479
			</span></i> (lyr.); also of the flute, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλυκὺν
				αὐλῶν ὄ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1202
			</span></i> (lyr.): pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄ. κροτάλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antim.
					<u>Eleg.Fr.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			.—The freq. Mss. reading <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀττοβέω, ὄττοβος</span> is disproved by the metre.
			(Onomatop.)</div>
